---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const cmsMode = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTENT_SOURCE === 'supabase';
---
<Layout title="About this project">
  <main id="main">
    <div class="page-intro"><h1>A place to explore. A reason to connect.</h1><p>A community website for Macon–Bibb.</p></div>
    <div class="prose"><h2>Two ways into the community</h2><p><a href="/maps/">Explore maps</a> to browse places, combine layers and see a different view of the area. Visit the <a href="/calendar/">community calendar</a> to browse dates, filter events and download a calendar file.</p>
    <h2>Community information and its sources</h2>{cmsMode ? <p>This release contains published event and map records. Follow each record’s source links and capture dates to confirm details with its publisher.</p> : <p>The calendar includes Macon, Bibb County and nearby-area events sourced from the Democratic Party of Georgia 26 feed on Mobilize, Mid GA DSA events from saved Google Calendar feeds, Middle Georgia Regional Library programs from CalendarWiz, and Bibb County School District events and academic dates. Follow the source links to confirm details with each organizer. The voting map uses uploaded polling-place and precinct data, including historical and unclassified records. The home page preview is drawn from the same voting data.</p>}<p>This site does not claim affiliation with Macon–Bibb County or any organization listed here. Use verified sources for event schedules, services and navigation.</p>
    <h2>Built to stay simple</h2>{cmsMode ? <p>Resident pages are a complete static snapshot. Staff API publication is separate from website deployment. No resident account or API connection is required to browse this release.</p> : <p>This is a static Astro website prepared for Cloudflare Pages. Event content and geographic layers can be updated as files and published with the next build. There is no account, event submission form or required application server.</p>}
    <h2>Explore your way</h2><p>The map’s place directory offers the same features as the selected geographic layers. Use it to find a place and show it on the map. The calendar provides both month and agenda views, source links and calendar downloads.</p><p><a href="/data/">See the datasets and sources</a>.</p></div>
  </main>
</Layout>
